@startuml virtual_delete_flow
' L9 reading page virtual Methods in Depth: what happens when a std::unique_ptr<Vehicle>
' that owns a Taxi deletes it through a Vehicle*. Measured with g++ 13.3 and
' AddressSanitizer on 2026-11-02 (the small Vehicle: two doubles and a virtual drive).
' Rendered to ../virtual_delete_flow.png at 300 dpi on white.
!theme mono
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Fira Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam dpi 300
start
:""delete"" through a ""Vehicle*""
that points to a ""Taxi"";
if (Is ""~Vehicle"" virtual?) then (yes)
  :1. ""~Taxi"" runs, then
""driver_name_"" is destroyed;
  :2. ""~Vehicle"" runs;
  :3. The whole ""Taxi"" is freed.
AddressSanitizer reports nothing;
else (no)
  #FFF3E0:**Undefined behavior**
With g++: only ""~Vehicle"" runs,
and AddressSanitizer reports
""new-delete-type-mismatch"":
56 bytes allocated,
deleted as 24 bytes;
endif
stop
@enduml
